WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.301
Rita, Justin, congratulations.

00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:03.936
You guys have made
it to the final round

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:05.304
of this competition.

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.307
Now it's time to send you
back to your home forges

00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:10.977
to recreate an iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:11.043 --> 00:00:17.550
That weapon is the sodegarami.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:18.551
Holy!

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:20.720
Geez!

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.321
Oh my god!

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:25.291
1, 2, 3.

00:00:25.357 --> 00:00:28.728
Today, we are protesting
the sodegarami.

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:31.697
I've tested long shafted
weapons before but nothing

00:00:31.797 --> 00:00:33.198
with this many spikes.

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:35.668
This weapon has
spikes everywhere.

00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:38.704
It's got spikes on the shaft,
all around, facing outwards.

00:00:38.771 --> 00:00:41.874
It's got hooks, and points,
and spikes facing at you.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:44.244
This weapon is spike-tacular.

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:46.846
I'm so excited to
use the sodegarami.

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:50.150
One of the most intimidating
and versatile Japanese pole

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:53.686
weapons, the sodegarami was part
of the key arsenal for samurai

00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:55.954
police during the 17th century.

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:57.957
Featuring lethal
spikes and hooks,

00:00:58.024 --> 00:01:00.359
police were able to
capture violent offenders

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.128
from a distance by
using the weapon

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:06.098
to latch onto the suspects,
stopping them in their tracks.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:08.034
Although primarily
used in defense,

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:10.336
the sharp spikes, along
with the spiked bud cap,

00:01:10.402 --> 00:01:13.540
made it a menacing and
brutal weapon when in combat.

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:16.209
Today, the sodegarami's
devastating use

00:01:16.275 --> 00:01:20.045
can be seen in the HBO
television series "Westworld."

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.181
It's got spikes everywhere
because it's supposed

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:24.584
to be a sleeve catcher--
something that when you

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:27.186
wield it and hit something, it's
supposed to catch on something.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.788
You bring it down, and
you spike him with it.

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:30.090
MAN: Action.

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:35.161
That is why we have
these pre-tests--

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:37.330
so that we find out
how to best bring

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:41.167
out the effectiveness of this
weapon according to its design.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.139
So, we use ballistics
dummies because it gives us

00:01:47.239 --> 00:01:51.210
the anatomy of the human body.

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:54.080
Feel of boom-- oh, that
penetrates deep into the guts.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.314
You're not going
to survive that.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.249
When you're cutting
into the skin,

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:57.784
oh, that's just not a cut.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:00.553
That actually crushed the
bones and into the heart.

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:02.622
So it's a very visual
thing to find out

00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:05.024
what kind of lethal
damage that weapon can

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:07.360
really do to the human body.

00:02:07.426 --> 00:02:09.729
My hand placement is
important because there

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:12.064
are spikes in areas that
if I put my hand there

00:02:12.164 --> 00:02:13.933
to make it lighter be
able to maneuver it,

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.002
I'm going to get spiked.

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:18.171
How do you use this thing?

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:20.540
And obviously, any way you want.

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:35.855
[chatter]

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:36.856
Have fun!

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:37.823
It's yours.

00:02:37.923 --> 00:02:38.991
Leave.

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:40.225
All right.

00:02:40.292 --> 00:02:41.761
It looks like it's
going to be fun to make.

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:42.795
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:43.897
We'll see you in four days.

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:49.334
My name is Rita Thurman.

00:02:49.401 --> 00:02:51.137 line:14%
I just turned 50 years old.

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:53.539 line:8%
I'm a scout leader, and
it's important for me

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:57.510 line:8%
to be here and be an example for
my scouts and for my daughter

00:02:57.576 --> 00:03:01.781
because I want them to try
things, even if it's hard.

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:04.450
I have never made
anything like this before.

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:08.221
I am going to start
with my entangler.

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:09.221
Super awesome.

00:03:09.321 --> 00:03:11.457
It's time for me to quench it.

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:16.128
Woo hoo!

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:18.464
My clench went well.

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:21.567
The head of the sodegarami
looks pretty good.

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.669
I'm feeling pretty good
after getting to spend

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:26.139
this time on the weapon.

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:27.740
I'm excited to see
that I could do it,

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:32.144
and I'm excited for my daughter
and my scouts to see too.

00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:34.146
Done pretty much
everything I wanted to do.

00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:37.016
I have time to do
one more thing--

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:38.150
stab.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:40.220
Attack a pumpkin Yoink!

00:03:43.989 --> 00:03:44.991
Oh no!

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:51.864
[gasps] Ah!

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:53.098
Oh [bleep].

00:03:53.198 --> 00:03:54.466
I got to fix this.

00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:55.467
Oh, no.

00:03:55.534 --> 00:03:56.435
[bleep]

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:58.003
I spent a lot of
time on this weapon,

00:03:58.070 --> 00:03:59.605
and I've broken this thing.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:03.109
So I'm just going to run back
and put whatever kind of crappy

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:04.409
weld I can get on it.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:05.912
If this doesn't
work, I'm screwed.

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:11.149
My name is Justin Harrington.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:12.819 line:8%
I'm from Clemons,
North Carolina.

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:15.254 line:8%
I've had one eye since
I was 12 years old,

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:16.522
and I've had a lot
of people tell me

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:19.892
what I can and can't do
in my life, and I just--

00:04:19.958 --> 00:04:21.894
I've never taken their advice.

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:23.562
I came on "Forged
in Fire" to show

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:25.364
other people with
physical limitations

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:27.400
that they're not limitations.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:30.569
They can be strengths.

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.071
So, we're going
to do a 15 and 20.

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:35.775
We'll clean at first, and
then we'll move on to our 1084

00:04:35.841 --> 00:04:36.943
and clean that up.

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:38.544
The next process
is going to be just

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:40.579
welding these bad boys together
and getting a billet together.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.615
I cut the billet
into four pieces.

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:45.318
I'm going to forge these
out into the four spikes

00:04:45.384 --> 00:04:46.585
in the front of the sodegarami.

00:04:46.685 --> 00:04:48.688
[chuckles] It's time to quench.

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:52.792
Go ahead and harden
just the blade,

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:54.960
leave the rest off so
that when they smack it

00:04:55.027 --> 00:04:56.963
into whatever they're going
to smack it in, hopefully

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:57.997
it won't break.

00:04:58.063 --> 00:05:00.032
A little Mongolian horsehair.

00:05:00.132 --> 00:05:01.668
That is a blood guard.

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:08.140
Putting the head
in, and it seems

00:05:08.206 --> 00:05:09.908
like it wanted to split on me.

00:05:09.975 --> 00:05:13.245
So we're going to throw a
little bit of epoxy and leather

00:05:13.345 --> 00:05:15.614
around this thing and
call it what it is.

00:05:15.714 --> 00:05:17.349
If something goes
wrong with my weapon,

00:05:17.416 --> 00:05:19.351
It's going to be that I
wasn't able to pin the head.

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:20.887
Just didn't have
the time to do it.

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:22.488
Hopefully, it stays together.

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:24.656
Sodegarami build is done.

00:05:24.723 --> 00:05:28.994
She might not be pretty,
but she will kill.

00:05:29.094 --> 00:05:30.095
All right, bladesmiths.

00:05:30.162 --> 00:05:32.731
Welcome to the kill test.

00:05:32.798 --> 00:05:36.102
To find out what kind of lethal
damage your sodegarami will do,

00:05:36.202 --> 00:05:37.603
I will take your
weapons and stab

00:05:37.703 --> 00:05:39.839
and try to snag this
ballistics dummy.

00:05:39.905 --> 00:05:41.707
Rita, you're up first.
You ready for this?

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:42.541
[japanese]

00:05:42.608 --> 00:06:10.903
All, right let's do this

00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:16.342
[laughs]

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:17.410
All right, Rita.

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:19.712
Let's talk about
your sodegarami.

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:21.980
The tines you have
here penetrates.

00:06:22.047 --> 00:06:25.384
The hook you have here
will rip this person apart.

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:28.921
And more importantly,
your weapon will kill.

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:30.489
Yes!

00:06:30.589 --> 00:06:31.590
All right, Justin.
Your turn.

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:32.758
You read to have fun?

00:06:32.825 --> 00:06:33.860
Yes, sir.

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:00.586
All right, Justin.

00:07:00.653 --> 00:07:03.823
The tines you have here,
it's more of a stabbing tine

00:07:03.923 --> 00:07:04.724
rather than a grabbing.

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:06.225
And this is a grabbing weapon.

00:07:06.292 --> 00:07:08.828
But that hook does
grab on to that.

00:07:08.894 --> 00:07:11.798
Overall, sir, your
weapon will kill.

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:17.703
All right, bladesmiths.

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:19.237
It's time for the
strength test--

00:07:19.304 --> 00:07:22.642
the dreaded ice block chop.

00:07:22.742 --> 00:07:24.443
Remember, this is not
about what these weapons

00:07:24.543 --> 00:07:26.545
do to the ice blocks
but what those ice

00:07:26.612 --> 00:07:28.280
blocks do to your weapons.

00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:29.849
And Rita, you're up first.

00:07:29.916 --> 00:07:32.184
You get points for
theme, I mean--

00:07:32.251 --> 00:07:35.087
[laughs] you ready?

00:07:35.187 --> 00:07:36.154
- A-ha.
- It doesn't matter.

00:07:36.221 --> 00:07:37.155
Right.

00:07:37.222 --> 00:07:38.558
No, it doesn't matter.

00:08:13.226 --> 00:08:14.727
All right, Rita.

00:08:14.793 --> 00:08:18.731
You got a little bit more of
a bend in this one tine here.

00:08:18.798 --> 00:08:22.401
But everything else is pretty
much the way it was going in.

00:08:22.467 --> 00:08:23.869
Definitely held up, did its job.

00:08:23.936 --> 00:08:24.837
Good job.

00:08:24.904 --> 00:08:26.305
- Thank you.
- All right, Justin.

00:08:26.371 --> 00:08:27.806
Your turn.
You ready?

00:08:27.873 --> 00:08:28.875
Yes, I am.

00:08:57.236 --> 00:08:59.605
All right, so, you
survived the strength test.

00:08:59.672 --> 00:09:02.808
This is a very strong,
well-built head for this.

00:09:02.908 --> 00:09:06.878
But it's built more like a
spear than it is for catching.

00:09:06.978 --> 00:09:09.081
I mean, I'm not sure
how effective it would

00:09:09.148 --> 00:09:11.116
be at snagging the opponent.

00:09:11.183 --> 00:09:12.685
But it's a devastator.

00:09:12.785 --> 00:09:14.186
It certainly did the job.

00:09:14.253 --> 00:09:15.221
Good job.

00:09:19.058 --> 00:09:20.426
All right, bladesmiths.

00:09:20.493 --> 00:09:25.030
Welcome to the sharpness test--
the sandman pierce and capture.

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:27.333
To test the sharpness,
I will take your weapon,

00:09:27.433 --> 00:09:29.702
pierce, and try to
control this sandman.

00:09:29.802 --> 00:09:30.703
Rita, you're up first.

00:09:30.803 --> 00:09:32.104
You ready for this?

00:09:32.204 --> 00:09:33.172
Yeah.

00:10:03.202 --> 00:10:04.370
All right, Rita.

00:10:04.437 --> 00:10:05.771
The points you have
on your tines here

00:10:05.838 --> 00:10:08.573
definitely penetrate when
you thrust into that.

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:10.376
But it doesn't
slice on the way out

00:10:10.442 --> 00:10:12.578
or capture as well as it should.

00:10:12.644 --> 00:10:14.847
Your hook over here did its job.

00:10:14.947 --> 00:10:18.451
Overall, it will
cut and control.

00:10:18.517 --> 00:10:20.052
All right, Justin your turn.
Are you ready?

00:10:20.152 --> 00:10:21.153
Yes, I am.

00:10:41.607 --> 00:10:42.842
Oh ho ho.

00:10:45.011 --> 00:10:46.045
That's not good.

00:10:49.981 --> 00:10:53.818
He pulled it
out of the socket.

00:10:53.919 --> 00:10:55.554
Well, Justin,
we have a problem.

00:10:55.621 --> 00:10:56.555
Yes, sir.

00:10:56.622 --> 00:10:57.856
This wasn't pinned, was it?

00:10:57.923 --> 00:10:59.024
No.

00:10:59.125 --> 00:11:01.326
The impact from all
these tests loosened it up.

00:11:01.393 --> 00:11:03.029
And of course, it came off.

00:11:06.098 --> 00:11:09.168
Justin, you brought in a
beautifully crafted weapon.

00:11:09.268 --> 00:11:11.670
However, you've suffered
a catastrophic failure

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:13.305
in our final test.

00:11:13.372 --> 00:11:17.042
And unfortunately, you cannot be
our "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:11:17.109 --> 00:11:18.577
- Congratulations, Rita.
- Thank you.

00:11:18.644 --> 00:11:20.012
Awesome.

00:11:20.079 --> 00:11:22.114
Coming on "Forged in Fire,"
I put my all into it,

00:11:22.181 --> 00:11:23.949
and I feel like I
made a good weapon.

00:11:24.015 --> 00:11:25.584
But just came up
short on a little bit

00:11:25.651 --> 00:11:28.154
of the fit and finish, and other
than that, I'm happy with it.

00:11:31.323 --> 00:11:32.758
Rita, congratulations.

00:11:32.858 --> 00:11:35.094
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:11:35.194 --> 00:11:38.497
and that is a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:11:38.564 --> 00:11:40.432
Congratulations.

00:11:40.532 --> 00:11:42.968
How do you feel right now?

00:11:43.068 --> 00:11:44.002
I just--

00:11:44.102 --> 00:11:46.405
Come on forward
and shake our hands.

00:11:46.505 --> 00:11:47.640
Good job.

00:11:47.706 --> 00:11:49.307
It's been a very
positive and uplifting

00:11:49.374 --> 00:11:52.578
experience to be able to do
something amazing like this.

00:11:52.645 --> 00:11:53.612
Thank you, you guys.

00:11:53.679 --> 00:11:55.815
Oh my god.

